@ref O 3 in the 1999 Revised Edition: the commencement day, paragraph 1 and paragraph 2 (src:TA1999-O3:21-37)
GIVEN `the equipment has been approved for sale by the Authority under regulation 24(1) of the Telecommunication (Dealers) Regulations (Rg 7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment is set out in the Fifth Schedule to the Telecommunication (Dealers) Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment meets the standards and specifications approved and published by the Authority from time to time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`O 3 para 2: the equipment is within the exemption` MEANS
        `the equipment has been approved for sale by the Authority under regulation 24(1) of the Telecommunication (Dealers) Regulations (Rg 7)`
    OR (`the equipment is set out in the Fifth Schedule to the Telecommunication (Dealers) Regulations` AND `the equipment meets the standards and specifications approved and published by the Authority from time to time`)

GIVEN reading IS A `What section 30 of the TAS Act provided`
      `the equipment has been approved for sale by the Authority under regulation 24(1) of the Telecommunication (Dealers) Regulations (Rg 7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment is set out in the Fifth Schedule to the Telecommunication (Dealers) Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment meets the standards and specifications approved and published by the Authority from time to time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`O 3 para 2: the equipment is exempt from the prohibition on possessing or operating equipment` MEANS
    CONSIDER reading
    WHEN `section 30(1) to (5) was the approval-before-use requirement` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `section 30(1) to (5) was the prohibition on possessing or operating equipment` THEN JUST (`O 3 para 2: the equipment is within the exemption` `the equipment has been approved for sale by the Authority under regulation 24(1) of the Telecommunication (Dealers) Regulations (Rg 7)` `the equipment is set out in the Fifth Schedule to the Telecommunication (Dealers) Regulations` `the equipment meets the standards and specifications approved and published by the Authority from time to time`)
    WHEN `the text of section 30 is not held` THEN NOTHING

GIVEN reading IS A `What section 30 of the TAS Act provided`
      `the equipment has been approved for sale by the Authority under regulation 24(1) of the Telecommunication (Dealers) Regulations (Rg 7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment is set out in the Fifth Schedule to the Telecommunication (Dealers) Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment meets the standards and specifications approved and published by the Authority from time to time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`O 3 para 2: the equipment is exempt from the approval-before-use requirement` MEANS
    CONSIDER reading
    WHEN `section 30(1) to (5) was the approval-before-use requirement` THEN JUST (`O 3 para 2: the equipment is within the exemption` `the equipment has been approved for sale by the Authority under regulation 24(1) of the Telecommunication (Dealers) Regulations (Rg 7)` `the equipment is set out in the Fifth Schedule to the Telecommunication (Dealers) Regulations` `the equipment meets the standards and specifications approved and published by the Authority from time to time`)
    WHEN `section 30(1) to (5) was the prohibition on possessing or operating equipment` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `the text of section 30 is not held` THEN NOTHING
